sections.s2_technical:
The OWNING SIDE is the entity that has the FK column in its table. In a one-to-many relationship between Account and Trade, the `trades` table has `account_id` FK. Therefore Trade is the owning side.

```java
// ═══ CHILD (Trade) — OWNING SIDE — has the FK column ═══
@Entity
@Table(name = "trades")
public class Trade {
    @Id
    @Column(name = "trade_id")
    private String tradeId;

    @ManyToOne(fetch = FetchType.LAZY)  // Many trades belong to ONE account
    @JoinColumn(name = "account_id", nullable = false)  // FK column in trades table
    private Account account;

    private String symbol;
    private BigDecimal amount;

    // Getters, setters...
}
// SQL: trades table has account_id column that references accounts(account_id)
```

```java
// ═══ PARENT (Account) — INVERSE SIDE — no FK column ═══
@Entity
@Table(name = "accounts")
public class Account {
    @Id
    @Column(name = "account_id")
    private String accountId;

    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "account", cascade = CascadeType.ALL, orphanRemoval = true)
    private List<Trade> trades = new ArrayList<>();
    // mappedBy = "account" → "Trade.account field owns this relationship"
    // cascade = ALL → persist/merge/remove propagate to trades
    // orphanRemoval = true → removing trade from list deletes it from DB

    private String holderName;
    private BigDecimal balance;

    // ═══ HELPER METHODS — synchronize BOTH sides ═══
    public void addTrade(Trade trade) {
        trades.add(trade);
        trade.setAccount(this);  // set the owning side!
    }

    public void removeTrade(Trade trade) {
        trades.remove(trade);
        trade.setAccount(null);  // clear the owning side!
    }
}
```

Why helper methods are CRITICAL:

```java
// (Avoid) WRONG: only set one side — the OTHER side is out of sync
account.getTrades().add(trade);  // inverse side updated
// trade.getAccount() is still null! JPA won't generate the FK!
// INSERT trades (trade_id, symbol, amount, account_id) VALUES (?, ?, ?, NULL) ← NULL FK!

// (Recommended) CORRECT: use helper that sets BOTH sides
account.addTrade(trade);
// trade.setAccount(account) called inside helper → FK is set!
// INSERT trades (..., account_id) VALUES (..., 'SAV2001') ← correct FK!
```

`@JoinColumn` attributes:

```java
@JoinColumn(
    name = "account_id",        // FK column name in THIS table
    nullable = false,            // NOT NULL constraint
    foreignKey = @ForeignKey(name = "fk_trade_account")  // custom FK constraint name
)
```

Unidirectional vs Bidirectional:

```java
// UNIDIRECTIONAL @ManyToOne: Trade → Account (child knows parent, parent doesn't know children)
// Simplest. No @OneToMany on Account. No mappedBy.
// Use when: you never need account.getTrades() — only trade.getAccount().

// BIDIRECTIONAL: Trade ↔ Account (both sides navigate)
// @ManyToOne on Trade + @OneToMany(mappedBy) on Account.
// Use when: you need both account.getTrades() AND trade.getAccount().

// UNIDIRECTIONAL @OneToMany (without @ManyToOne): Account → trades
// (Caution) AVOID: JPA creates a JOIN TABLE (accounts_trades) instead of a FK!
// Less efficient. Always prefer bidirectional or @ManyToOne unidirectional.
```

